    <string name="manage_skip_certificates">Equipment whose certificate cannot be checked</string>
    <string name="manage_skip_certificates_hint">Hosts or addresses, separated by commas. Some equipment ships a certificate issued for 127.0.0.1, which can never be valid for the address it is reached at. For a host listed here the certificate is not checked, so anything that can answer at that address can pretend to be it: the connection is still encrypted, but it is no longer proof of who answered. Only a skill reaching its own endpoint is let through this; fetching a link out of mail always checks.</string>
